    "answer": {
      "short": "$a\\in\\mathbb{R},\\quad b=1$.",
      "worked": "Both polynomial branches are continuous on their respective intervals, so only $x=0$ needs checking.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(0)&=1\\\\f_L(0)&=b\\\\f_R(0)&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nContinuity requires $f(0)=f_L(0)=f_R(0)$, so $b=1$. The value of $a$ does not affect $f_L(0)$, so $a$ can be any real number.\n\nThus $a\\in\\mathbb{R}$ and $b=1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
